    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0140" n="90" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg90"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Gana.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your note
                    of the 28th ultimo, submitting the suggestion of your Government that the claims
                    not decided by the American Chilean commission, which recently sat at
                    Washington, be adjusted by paying such an amount of the face of such claims as
                    the aggregate amount awarded by the commission on claims which they did consider
                    bears to the face amount of the latter claims.</p>
                <pb facs="0141" n="91" xml:id="pg91"/>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say to your excellency that this Government does not
                    feel warranted in consenting to such an arrangement. It thinks that each and
                    every claim should be examined and settled upon its merits, by an international
                    commission.</p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Minister, the renewed assurance of my highest consideration.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
